<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- An NPC that hunts ships of certain purposes takes every player's own ship as a target as it takes player 1's
     (native_gate_player_groups, a session default: this patch ships with md/setup.xml's,
     tools/dev/native_gate_player_groups.xml).

     X4's search for enemies (aiscripts/move.seekenemies.xml) serves the hunters that look for ships of given purposes:
     pirates of the Plunder order and Yaki raiders (trade and mining ships carrying their basket's wares), recon and
     police with target purposes. Its rule for "the ship the player flies" is that it always has a valid purpose, since
     nobody knows what the player does with it. A hunter that takes its target straight from what its radar found (a
     basket hunter, a recon) then takes the player's ship; one that ranks its targets (lib.target.selection.xml) filters
     by purpose again, for player 1 too. The script is the hunter's and runs outside every player's scope, where
     `player` is player 1, so a player 2..N's own ship had to pass the purpose test: in a fighter or a miner with a
     pirate's wares on board it was never picked (24 Nov playtest, player 2: the enemies seemed to act differently).
     Two sites: the gravidar condition that wakes the hunter, and the filter of what it found.
     Here the ship any player controls is also "the ship the player flies" (the player groups keep that table on every
     player's entity on every client at the same ticks: $X4LAN_Pilots, from each player's controlled object to that
     player's entity; X4 keeps no script variables on a ship, and AI scripts read no MD globals). Player 1's own ship
     passes by the stock clause as before; without the gate nothing sets the table and every line is the stock one.
     Our own clauses only; the stock script is patched in memory by X4's own diff loading, never on disk. -->
<diff>
 <replace sel="//check_value[@value='@$detected.{$i} == player.occupiedship']/@value">@$detected.{$i} == player.occupiedship or @player.entity.$X4LAN_Pilots.{$detected.{$i}}</replace>
 <replace sel="//do_elseif[@value='$targetpurposes.count and not $targetpurposes.indexof.{$locobject.primarypurpose} and ($locobject != player.occupiedship)']/@value">$targetpurposes.count and not $targetpurposes.indexof.{$locobject.primarypurpose} and ($locobject != player.occupiedship) and not @player.entity.$X4LAN_Pilots.{$locobject}</replace>
</diff>
